nd on on the floor  we're required to wear a mask  on the house floor and in the committee  hearings ironically that's where the tv  cameras are so this is purely theater  apparently kovit works differently in  both chambers  because in the senate you don't wear a  mask in the house you have to wear a  mask  the only difference is the speaker she  doesn't want to abide by the cdc rules  she actually wants to have greater  control  trey i suspect this is one of those  things that makes you not miss  being on capitol hill in the house  one of a trillion shannon there were a  lot of rules when i was in the house and  they were usually honored only in their  breach  we weren't supposed to bring drinks on  the house floor we weren't supposed to  take pictures  almost everyone violated those i did not  i'm a rule follower which  which kind of brings me to my larger  point anyone can follow a rule they  agree  they agree with i mean it takes no  courage to follow a rule you agree with  it's those that we don't agree with that  separates the law and order people from  everyone else so if you don't like the  rule  then retake the house and change the  rules or  honor it or if you're gonna break it and  engage in civil disobedience pay your  dadgum fine  those are your three options honor the  rule change the rule  or engage in civil disobedience but pay  your fine if you're going to do so  i'm glad i'm not the only one still  using the phrase dadgum uh it was used  very nicely there dre  matthew what about this um you know  people who are saying i'll pay the fine  i'll do whatever well what about this  accusation from members that it's only  within tv  camera range that the masks are mandated  it's obvious that this is political on  pelosi's part she wants to punish the  members mainly republicans who haven't  taken the vaccine when in fact they're  only  endangering themselves by not taking the  by not having the vaccination  it's very politicized and partisan and  it only 